// Wave 1 acceptance: self-target shield ability.
// Lowers to AbilityProgram { gate: { cooldown_ticks: 40, range: 0.0 },
//                            effects: [EffectOp::Shield { amount: 50.0 }],
//                            stackings: [Some(StackingMode::Stack)],
//                            lifetimes: [Some(LifetimeMode::DamageableHp(50.0))] }
//
// `stacking stack` exercises Wave 1.5#3 stacking-mode lowering — on
// recast, the .sim's ApplyShield does
// `new_shield = agents.shield_hp(t) + a` (additive accumulation),
// which IS stack semantics. Registry-driven stacking dispatch is later
// infrastructure; the binding-check asserts the lowered slot matches
// the .sim's natural additive behavior.
//
// `damageable_hp(50)` exercises Wave 1.5#8 lifetime-modifier lowering
// — the buff has 50 hp of absorption capacity that drains as incoming
// damage hits; when shield_hp reaches 0 the buff is "broken". The
// .sim's ApplyDamage already drains shield_hp on hit
// (`absorbed = min(s, d_scaled); s = s - absorbed`) and naturally
// settles at 0 when the pool empties — that IS DamageableHp(N)
// semantics. The binding-check asserts the lowered value matches the
// .sim's natural drain behavior; registry-driven lifetime dispatch
// is later infrastructure.

ability ShieldUp {
    target: self
    cooldown: 4s
    hint: defense

    shield 50 stacking stack [DEFENSE: 100] damageable_hp(50)
}
